  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of Protection Assistance and Improved Access to Essential Services for Internally Displaced People (IDPs) in Informal Settlements in Iraq</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Five years after the end of large-scale military operations against the Islamic State of Iraq and Levant (ISIL), the humanitarian situation in Iraq remains fragile, characterised by protracted internal displacement, eroded social cohesion and incomplete rehabilitation of housing, basic services, and livelihood opportunities. Through this project, IOM is contributing to preventing, reducing, and mitigating protection threats for internally displaced persons (IDPs) living in protracted displacement in informal settlements in Iraq with increased access to services through an integrated protection response. The Action is providing direct legal services, including counselling and representation and protection case management including gender-based violence (GBV) services. Additionally, IOM aims to increase protection capacity of the affected population and their access to basic services through information and referrals to services as well as procedure-related information on accessing civil documentation. IOM is also providing financial support and emergency cash intervention to IDPs, in particular those at risk of eviction GBV. IOM is also conducting protection monitoring for evidence-based programming and advocacy. Lastly, IOM is improving the capacity of national organisations to provide specialized protection.</narrative>
  </description>
